{"audio": "romans-12.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 144800, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2000, "text": "Romans, Chapter Twelve."}, {"start_ms": 2000, "end_ms": 11867, "text": "I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service."}, {"start_ms": 11867, "end_ms": 23867, "text": "And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God."}, {"start_ms": 23867, "end_ms": 37600, "text": "For I say, through the grace given unto me, to every man that is among you, not to think of himself more highly than he ought to think; but to think soberly, according as God hath dealt to every man the measure of faith."}, {"start_ms": 37600, "end_ms": 47200, "text": "For as we have many members in one body, and all members have not the same office: So we, being many, are one body in Christ, and every one members one of another."}, {"start_ms": 47200, "end_ms": 64133, "text": "Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, let us prophesy according to the proportion of faith; Or ministry, let us wait on our ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching; Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth,"}, {"start_ms": 64133, "end_ms": 70533, "text": "let him do it with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that sheweth mercy, with cheerfulness."}, {"start_ms": 70533, "end_ms": 72933, "text": "Let love be without dissimulation."}, {"start_ms": 72933, "end_ms": 76933, "text": "Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good."}, {"start_ms": 76933, "end_ms": 96133, "text": "Be kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honour preferring one another; Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord; Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer; Distributing to the necessity of saints; given to hospitality."}, {"start_ms": 96133, "end_ms": 99600, "text": "Bless them which persecute you: bless, and curse not."}, {"start_ms": 99600, "end_ms": 103067, "text": "Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep."}, {"start_ms": 103067, "end_ms": 105867, "text": "Be of the same mind one toward another."}, {"start_ms": 105867, "end_ms": 110400, "text": "Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate."}, {"start_ms": 110400, "end_ms": 112667, "text": "Be not wise in your own conceits."}, {"start_ms": 112667, "end_ms": 115600, "text": "Recompense to no man evil for evil."}, {"start_ms": 115600, "end_ms": 118133, "text": "Provide things honest in the sight of all men."}, {"start_ms": 118133, "end_ms": 123333, "text": "If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men."}, {"start_ms": 123333, "end_ms": 133333, "text": "Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 133333, "end_ms": 141200, "text": "Therefore if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head."}, {"start_ms": 141200, "end_ms": 144800, "text": "Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good."}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 545, "e": 1010, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1293, "e": 1636, "si": 0}, {"t": "Twelve.", "s": 1677, "e": 2000, "si": 0}, {"t": "I", "s": 2761, "e": 2781, "si": 1}, {"t": "beseech", "s": 2821, "e": 3261, "si": 1}, {"t": "you", "s": 3301, "e": 3381, "si": 1}, {"t": "therefore,", "s": 3421, "e": 3841, "si": 1}, {"t": "brethren,", "s": 3881, "e": 4242, "si": 1}, {"t": "by", "s": 4302, "e": 4422, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 4442, "e": 4522, "si": 1}, {"t": "mercies", "s": 4582, "e": 4942, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 4982, "e": 5062, "si": 1}, {"t": "God,", "s": 5142, "e": 5482, "si": 1}, {"t": "t